cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Fabius: one set of operating rules above every model — a plugin, not a platform"
message: "If you cite this work, please cite the whitepaper in paper/fabius-as-a-system.pdf."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shemesh
    given-names: Ariel
abstract: >-
  A fifteen-skill agent architecture with a router that dispatches by
  layer, machinery and model tier over an always-on lean core. The
  decision core is twenty-two routing rules, each carrying a proof of
  the mathematics beneath it, together with a coherence theorem stating
  that the core composes into one consistent, complete and composable
  decision system, exceptions printed rather than omitted. Each of the
  twenty-six formal statements was written by one agent and then
  adversarially reviewed by an independent verifier whose only task was
  to find an error; that pass corrected ten of them before publication.
  Proof blocks are classed real-math or qualitative (22 and 4
  respectively) and every rule is fabius's own — derived and
  adversarially verified, proved where a proof is claimed and labelled
  heuristic where it is not.
  Evaluation is one reproducible benchmark in four panels, including a
  blind-judged quality panel across four Claude tiers and the versioned
  hundred-task FBS suite run BASE, FAB and FAB_MEMORY.
version: 2.6.2
repository-code: "https://github.com/shear559/fabius"
